<title>CHILE: Chile financial sector 10-mth net up 5.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Chile financial sector 10-mth net up 5.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's financial system reported net earnings of 186.9 million pesos in the first 10 months of the year, up 5.8 percent from the same period in 1995, said the Banking and Financial Institutions Superintendency.  Total loan portfolios grew 13.4 percent last month against the same period 1995.</p>
<p>Highest growth was seen in consumer loans, up 32 percent, followed by housing credits, up 24 percent and commercial loans which increased 15 percent.</p>
<p>Following are net earnings of individual banks in the 10 months of the year to October compared with a year earlier.  </p>
<p>			   Oct 1996	     Oct 1995</p>
<p>Banco Bhif		10.81		   n/a</p>
<p>Banco de A. Edwards   15.47		   6.5</p>
<p>Banco de Chile	  19.79		   n/a</p>
<p>Banco de Credito	18.16		   n/a</p>
<p>Banco Santiago	  10.22		   n/a</p>
<p>Banco O'Higgins	 18.09		  14.4</p>
<p>Banco Santander-Chile 26.25		   n/a</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures are in billions of pesos. The October 1995 figures are in peso terms from that month and are not expressed in 1996 pesos.</p>
<p>-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212</p>
